PASS: 11/11 claims, 2s
  [PASS] pass_qc is True on all 1,984,900 rows of the published constraint table -- the column is a constant, so a QC failure appears as an ABSENT row, never as pass_qc = False
  [PASS] the window set is the paper's: 1,984,900 autosomal windows, 141,341 coding-overlapping and 1,843,559 exclusively noncoding (Methods: 1,984,900 / 141,341 / 1,843,559)
  [PASS] the two tables partition cleanly: 2,572,802 autosomal step-1 windows = 1,984,900 scored + 587,902 absent
  [PASS] every one of the 2,572,802 windows has all three QC inputs on file (0 missing a pass fraction, a coverage or a possible count), so the filter can be re-evaluated everywhere rather than assumed
  [PASS] FORWARD DIRECTION: all 1,984,900 scored windows satisfy the published filter when it is re-evaluated from the raw pass/coverage/possible inputs -- 0 violate it, so nothing was admitted in spite of the rule the Methods state
  [PASS] the margins agree: over the scored set the pass fraction bottoms out at 0.8000, coverage spans 25.003-34.862 and `possible` bottoms out at 1,000 -- and the 1,723 windows at exactly 0.8 confirm the comparison is >=, not >
  [PASS] REVERSE DIRECTION: 98.1% of absent windows fail at least one of the paper's three conditions (threshold 95%); the residual 10,921 pass all three and are unexplained, so the filter is not a complete account of membership
  [PASS] absence is the PASS-fraction rule, not missing coverage: 417,097 windows fail >= 80% PASS against 19,396 failing the 25-35x band -- so 'no gnomAD coverage' is the wrong name for this stratum
  [PASS] the same holds site-weighted, which is what panel C's third band counts: of its 537,985 sites, 87.8% are in windows failing the PASS rule against 1.0% failing coverage
  [PASS] the QC-fail stratum is a MIXTURE, not the noncoding remainder: 40,509 of its 587,902 windows overlap coding exons and 547,393 do not, with a coding_prop on file for every one
  [PASS] and its coding share, 6.9%, is within 2 points of the QC-pass windows' 7.1% -- QC failure is close to independent of coding status, so panel C's third band is not a coding band in disguise
